                <pb facs="0390" n="348" xml:id="pg348"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">No. 155</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>On February 2, President Truman directed
                    that the results of the recently-concluded talks with Prime Minister Pleven “be reported by the Department of State
                    for the information of the National Security Council.” As a result of this
                    directive, Acheson forwarded a memorandum
                    to NSC Executive Secretary Lay on February 23 entitled “Results of the
                    Conversations Between the President and the French Prime Minister.” Lay circulated this memorandum immediately to
                    the members of the National Security Council, the Secretary of the Treasury, and
                    the Director of Defense Mobilization as NSC 105.
                    Documentation concerning NSC 105 is in S/S-NSC files, lot
                    63D351, NSC 105 Memoranda.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
